{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed","id":986606,"title":"How does your character feed?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-12T23:49:14-07:00","id":986606,"title":"How does your character feed?","content":"Pretty much what it says in the title. What's your vampire's MO for feeding, and what clan are they?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T00:54:16-07:00","id":986621,"title":"","content":"(Nosferatu) Obfuscate + Vigor = By the time anybody notices their friend is missing from the group, I'll be long gone... or maybe I'm hungry enough for seconds!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:35:39-07:00","id":986634,"title":"","content":"Crazy straw and a knife.<br /> <br /> <i>(May not actually be a vampire)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T01:41:30-07:00","id":986635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=986621#post986621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Nosferatu) Obfuscate + Vigor = By the time anybody notices their friend is missing from the group, I'll be long gone... or maybe I'm hungry enough for seconds!</div> </div> </div> </div>So the sneaky/violent approach. You're killing the victims, or just leave them in a corner dazzled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:55:22-07:00","id":986653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=986635#post986635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the sneaky/violent approach. You're killing the victims, or just leave them in a corner dazzled?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on how the night goes. Being drugged could explain one of their friends having no memory of what happened after they were plucked off the streets. But killing them might also be the safer alternative. Especially if I hide the body somewhere like the sewers, in a dumpster, or even up in a tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2016, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T04:26:42-07:00","id":986673,"title":"","content":"Doesn't that play havoc with your Humanity scores?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T04:30:28-07:00","id":986676,"title":"","content":"I play a Julii member of the Undead Legion so Dominate. Dominate. Dominate. But more specifically he drops by people's homes in the middle class housing areas, pretending to be city watch, and preys on whoever answers the door. The old Impersonating an Officer trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10827-baronzobops","name":"baronzobops","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10827_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:08:33-07:00","id":986770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=986673#post986673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't that play havoc with your Humanity scores?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does at first. But the lower your humanity is, the worse actions are needed to weaken it further. Eventually occasional murder won't really affect you.<br /> <br /> Mass murder, on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2016, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T08:42:10-07:00","id":986782,"title":"","content":"I ran, didn't play. Most of my players at some point had merits that allowed for feeding through Hunting Grounds and stuff. Most commonly blood was obtained through subtle means, usually at I guess what would be called a Rack, a bar where vampires tend to hang out with suitably dark lighting. Sometimes Obfuscate was used to feed on sleeping people, or Dominate when they were running by and needed a quick fill up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:47:07-07:00","id":986844,"title":"","content":"The vampires in my game often use the subtle feeding in nightclubs and bars. A few times they have dominated someone to let them. One of the vampires... is feeding off the other vampires in the group who let him. <br /> <br /> A few do it during sexual encounters. <br /> One does it through brute force, just snatches someone up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:54:52-07:00","id":986847,"title":"","content":"Grindr. It's like ordering delivery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T12:44:38-07:00","id":986897,"title":"","content":"My least Requiem character was a Mekhet Private Investigator, Circle of the Crone who was Embraced because as a mortal he had developed Shadow Contacts, and that interested his Crone Sire. If I had played him in 2nd, he'd have been Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> He fed via a series of affairs/black-mail of clients/subjects under the ruse of &quot;sexual favors&quot;. A strange type of Casanova to be sure, but reliable way to keep a herd in check as it removes for some the pretense of mutual amorous feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T16:07:49-07:00","id":986994,"title":"","content":"Order lots of takeout for the mortal and ghoul enterage, and have a snack for myself.<br /> <br /> Plenty of social dots and Ill gotten majesty discipline. <br /> <br /> -Kayla Sworn of the Mysteries Scholar of the Wyrm Paris Hilton of Clan Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:44:00-07:00","id":987038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed#post986606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much what it says in the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>With their fangs, usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:00:34-07:00","id":987051,"title":"","content":"Is that you, Ephsy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T19:46:05-07:00","id":987067,"title":"","content":"Ventrue of the Ordo Dracul, just uses Dominate to grab a bite and make the person forget all about it. It's quick, simple, and doesn't rely on seduction tactics he's no good at. Prefers not to kill because he dwells in a small town setting where that draws the wrong kind of attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T01:06:16-07:00","id":987139,"title":"","content":"Old people's homes, intensive care units of hospitals, retirement communities. Anywhere that people might be expected to die or fall ill and tired naturally.<br /> <br /> Got the idea from a former house mate who hoped there would be a pandemic of bird flu or similar because it would wipe out elderly and sick people (she said) which &quot;we didn't need&quot;. She reminded me how predators go for the weakest in the herd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T01:38:59-07:00","id":987151,"title":"","content":"I'm about to start playing a gangrel who either feeds on her mystery cult adherants (claiming that the spilling of their blood brings them closer to the spirit they worship as a god), preys on weak spirits, or if she has to go after something else she defaults to the violent method in an alleyway or someone's house or their car. Sometimes she'll awkwardly make her way through the nightclub scene but that typically ends with her just feeling out of place and getting nowhere or a guy says the wrong thing and has a rib or two broken and she still gets nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:12:55-07:00","id":987220,"title":"","content":"How do story tellers deal with the Dominating and feeding because feeding would break Dominate. So suddenly there would be this person sucking on their neck and they dont remember how exactly that happened, I would think more often than not the victim would panic even if it felt good...( some cases, that would be the cause of the panic )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:09:27-07:00","id":987240,"title":"","content":"I go with 'the Kiss keeps them docile when they come out of it long enough to use Dominate to cover it up again.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:41:31-07:00","id":987271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=987220#post987220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do story tellers deal with the Dominating and feeding because feeding would break Dominate. So suddenly there would be this person sucking on their neck and they dont remember how exactly that happened, I would think more often than not the victim would panic even if it felt good...( some cases, that would be the cause of the panic )</div> </div> </div> </div>You use Dominate AFTER you feed from them.<br /> <br /> Use Dominate to have them follow you. Proceed to feed. (Mesmerize is broken but the Kiss is now in effect.) Mesmerize again and adjust memories as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T04:31:38-07:00","id":988783,"title":"","content":"Now that my Nosferatu can only feed from vampires, I found someone who had no legs or arms, and had them Embraced.<br /> <br /> Now, they hang on my wall. I feed them whatever I can scrounge around (rats, dogs, cats, bums, etc.), and I then feed off of them.<br /> <br /> You know, I think I can get into this recycling thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:00:17-07:00","id":988814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=988783#post988783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that my Nosferatu can only feed from vampires, I found someone who had no legs or arms, and had them Embraced.<br /> <br /> Now, they hang on my wall. I feed them whatever I can scrounge around (rats, dogs, cats, bums, etc.), and I then feed off of them.<br /> <br /> You know, I think I can get into this recycling thing...</div> </div> </div> </div>So what are you gonna do about the blood bond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:33:38-07:00","id":988850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=988814#post988814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are you gonna do about the blood bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if his BP is high enough that he has to feed from vampires, and he's feeding from relatively young neonates, he does get a considerable bonus to resist being bonded (it's not automatic in 2E - AFB, so can't give you a page quote).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:41:16-07:00","id":988854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=988850#post988850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if his BP is high enough that he has to feed from vampires, and he's feeding from relatively young neonates, he does get a considerable bonus to resist being bonded (it's not automatic in 2E - AFB, so can't give you a page quote).</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Potency 6+ makes you immune to vitae addiction. High blood potency helps you resist the bond. A blood potency 6 vampire gets to roll 6 - vitae imbibed dice to resist it at the cost of a point of willpower. Any <i>further</i> attempts apply an additional -1 to your roll, meaning that even high blood potency kindred are eventually going to succumb if they keep drinking from the same vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:13:07-07:00","id":988863,"title":"","content":"Cruac 4, for all your elder-feeding needs. Though, given how much time and vitae that requires, that's almost a zero sum game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:33:35-07:00","id":988873,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> I'm not really asking &quot;How does an elder get around the requirement,&quot; but specifically asking what Azenogoth does to get around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-17-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:17:53-07:00","id":988889,"title":"","content":"Probably kill the quadriplegic once he starts feeling an iota of sympathy for it, make another quadriplegic revenant and chain it up ad nauseum. He's not losing his Humanity rating at this point, particularly if he banes out this particular brand of sadism in the name of self preservation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:26:52-07:00","id":988918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=988889#post988889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably kill the quadriplegic once he starts feeling an iota of sympathy for it, make another quadriplegic revenant and chain it up ad nauseum. He's not losing his Humanity rating at this point, particularly if he banes out this particular brand of sadism in the name of self preservation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once you are blood bonded .. killing your Regnant becomes a breaking point. Especially if you wait until BB3 then it is at humanity 1... It takes more of a toll on your soul than spree killing mass murdering and surviving centuries.. How do you get passed this? <br /> <br /> Also BP 6+ vampires can take &quot;unnatural affinity&quot; and try to feed from werewolves or changelings or whatever oddball creature that you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:44:30-07:00","id":988924,"title":"","content":"Chaining up revenants in your basement, since they can't form blood bonds, is generally a good practice. They can always feed on animals and blood packs so you can fill them up when you need to feed. It's also a pretty ethically horrible thing to do, but from a pragmatic standpoint it's good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:07:37-07:00","id":988968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=988814#post988814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what are you gonna do about the blood bond?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Coil of the Voivod is a wonderful thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now my Humanity rating, however, that is a completely different story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T12:27:32-07:00","id":988977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=988918#post988918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Once you are blood bonded .. killing your Regnant becomes a breaking point. Especially if you wait until BB3 then it is at humanity 1... It takes more of a toll on your soul than spree killing mass murdering and surviving centuries.. How do you get passed this?<br /> <br /> Also BP 6+ vampires can take &amp;quot;unnatural affinity&amp;quot; and try to feed from werewolves or changelings or whatever oddball creature that you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bane mechanics were specifically designed to allow players to have characters to indulge precisely this sort of unregenerate behavior without flushing Humanity entirely. As has been pointed out, revenants don't form blood bonds. My rationale for killing them sporadically is so you (the character) don't become attached to them or susceptible to letting them get the chance to successfully talk you into releasing them. (And running the risk of your depravity becoming publicized.) But honestly you'd likely get the same results of a gilded cage. Promise someone virtual immortality and a life of luxury on the condition they never leave your estate without you and then embrace/semi embrace them. Then proceed to let them live it up on your dime. But vampires seem to have difficulty with the concept of catching more flies with honey than vinegar.<br /> <br /> I agree provisionally the unnatural affinity would probably be a better investment but if the odd supernaturals don't exist in your chronicle, then the merit isn't feasible... and if they do, hunting and/or caging them up is riskier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-18-2016, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T03:55:08-07:00","id":989282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=986847#post986847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grindr. It's like ordering delivery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know, I never considered that, but my characters could totally use grindr to catfish and get a ready supply of food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:39:32-07:00","id":989350,"title":"","content":"One nos I wrote up for my Savannah setting feed from her private ghost tour groups, using obfuscate and nightmare to make it seem like a haunting out of control had assaulted them, which then ensured a good review and that they would take the tour again next they were in the city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:23:58-08:00","id":1004952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986606-how-does-your-character-feed?p=989282#post989282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You know, I never considered that, but my characters could totally use grindr to catfish and get a ready supply of food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to be honest, considering the vampires of this setting, it's not much different from an ordinary Grindr hookup, minus the blood loss.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:29:57-08:00","id":1004959,"title":"","content":"I had a Ventrue who was addicted to the taste of fear. They struggle a little, and then his fangs sink in. The taste of blood mixed with fear was exhilarating, and ever since, he never fed any other way.<br /> <br /> Specializes in Nightmare despite his Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}